>Thomas Wright (t-mas@uhhep.phys.uh.edu) wrote:
>> 	We have been looking ant adding disk space to our DEC 3000/300X running
>> OSF/1 v2.0. The system admin. book says that OSF/1 supports the RZ74, but DEC
>> says that it is unsupported. Has anyone tried to put one of these on an Alpha
>> yet? If so, did you run into any problems? Has anyone added any other 3GB or
>> larger disks?

yes,  we have a 4GB disk from Resolv on our DEC 4000.
It seems that alphas can interactively quiz the disk drive
to find out its size and configure it.  The manuals didn't tell me this,
but lots of phone calls to DEC UK did.  (And I honestly do appreciate it,
so I'll refrain from speculating why DEC doesn't make this more widely known).

You do the disklabel & newfs as follows:

disklabel -rw /dev/rrz8c /dev/rrz8c
newfs /dev/rrz8c /dev/rrz8c

piece of cake.

