Summary: can an object possess 2 interfaces at the same time?
Keywords: OSF DCE type manager interface

can an object possess 2 interfaces, i.e. 2 responsible type
managers,  at the same time?

idea:
an object has a 
  - type-specific interface, f.i. enter_date, and at the same time
  - a type-independent interface, f.i. get_usage_info.

the type manager implementing the type-independent interface is
attached to every object in addition to the type-specific manager.

