On many platforms, the program known as "awk" is actually "nawk":  this
has been the case with both SunOS/Solaris and HP-UX for at least 1 or 2
years now.

The easiest way to find out the state of awk on your system is to write
a script using nawk syntax elements not found in awk, and run it through
awk:  if it barfs, it's awk; if not, it's nawk.

