In article <17021B887S86.UC577050@mizzou1.missouri.edu>, UC577050@mizzou1.missouri.edu (Ramana Turlapati) writes:
> Hello DCE programmers/developers,
> I have a few questions regarding setting up mutual authentication
> between a client and server.
>  
> I have it setup now wherein both server/client contact the security
> registry server to authenticate each others principals. I am right

I am a bit confuesd as to what you are trying to accomplish here. When
a client makes a protected-RPC to a server all the mutual
authentication stuff happens in the runtime automatically so that when
your server wakes up in the manager routine - the client is
authenticated to it.

> now passing a value of NULL for registry site argument to get the
> binding handle. If the client happens to opearte in a different cell, how
> can server know about the regisrty server of the client? Similarly how
> can a client authenticate a server in a different cell?
>  

I think the call you should be making here is
rpc_binding_set_auth_info() and not a sec_rgy call (which I think you
are doing). The 2nd argument is the name of the server, which can be a
principal name in your cell ("server") or a principal name in a foreign
cell ("/.../foreign-cell/server"). 

If this doesn't help, be more specific next time around with the APIs
that you are using.

Jonathan
