In article <Cun8LB.D16@da_vinci.ecte.uswc.uswest.com>, jmsewel@makedust.mtt.it.uswc.uswest.com (Justin M. Sewell) writes:
> Is there a limit to the value that can be specified for the max_calls_exec 
> parameter on the DCE rpc_server_listen() call?   In other words, if I specify
> 50000 for max_calls_exec I would actually get 50000 call threads?

My hunch is that since you would be doing the equivalent of 50000
pthread_create() calls + setting up a fairly large call-queue in the
runtime,  that you would eventually run out of memory. Keep in mind
that every call thread has its own stack carved out of VM with a
default size of 32-64KB. At 32KB/stack that is 1562 GB of VM for stack
alone...

