Wolfgang Lux (lux@gmdzi.gmd.de) wrote:
: Questions:
: - where does the idl put the interface uuid contained in the idl-file?
:   I did not find it in the stub sources.


        A client looks for the interface in the following manner:
        1.  Looks for the entry in CDS namespace, first. If you are
        not using CDS namespace, then your binding method has to be
        explicit in the idl file.

        2. UUID is given in the header file.h.  The marshalling
        routines are in file_cstub/stsub as the case may be.

        3. For your problem, make sure that you have your function
        name entered in the entry point manager
        you have to say something like rpcfunctionnameManagerepv = ...
        etc in your server. When the server gets into the interface
        it braggs only about its own functions.  Clients will be able
	to find only these functions/interfaces.
                                                               
