The interface uuid is part of the interface handle, or ifspec. You can
find the construction of it at the end of the server stub code for
your interface. The uuid is encoding in hex pairs into the ifspec.

Without looking at your code it is hard to figure out what is wrong
(boy, isn't that a brilliant one :-)), but you might check and see
that your problematic object is mapped to a manager type that is in
fact registered with your interface (via rpc_object_set_type). Also,
