In article <3326i0$p1o@gmdzi.gmd.de>, lux@gmdzi.gmd.de (Wolfgang Lux) writes:
> I have written a small dce server, providing 2 objects with
> one interface and different type managers and 1 object with
> a diffent interface.
> There is no problem using the first two objects.
> When using the third object I get the error message:
> Exception: unknown interface (dce / rpc)
> 
> Questions:
> - where does the idl put the interface uuid contained in the idl-file?
>   I did not find it in the stub sources.
> 

In your idl file, as generated by using the UUIDGEN, you will see an
interface header and interface body. Typically, the idl file looks like:

[ interface header] interface INTERFACENAME
{ <RPC operations> }


Possible explainations (just a guess since it is difficult to explain
something without first looking at the codes) are:
 
(1) In your server initilization routine, the 'other object UUID' is not
    registered uniquely / correctly with the CDS.
(2) In searching for that 'other object UUID', the rpc_ns_binding_lookup_
    routine cannot find the binding information as requested by the client.
    Check your search criteria / specification.


You may find it helpful to examine comm_status and fault_status return
codes in the exceptional handler.

Good luck.
 
