different things, none of which have worked.  I've also tried the following C
program that I just wrote, which works fine until it's connected to the print
queue.  I've come to the conclusion that the computer is simply ignoring
whatever I tell it, possibly because it's printing through the network.

I set up the print queue using 'lprsetup'.  Here's what it created for a
printcap entry.

lp4|4|test:\
	:if=/usr/local/bin/psfilter:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lp4err:\
	:lp=:\
	:of=/usr/local/bin/psfilter:\
	:rm=serts:\
	:rp=lp:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd4:

As far as I can tell, though, a file would be simply sent to the printer
without ever passing through the filter.  Am I supposed to reboot or something?

Probably I'm just missing something.  I'm not exactly an expert in this stuff.
I'd appreciate any help you can give me.

Thank you,

