>Does anyone have an explanation for this behavior?

Patch id:       OSFV20-014-1

Setting LD_LIBRARY_PATH with a redundant path will result in /sbin/loader
suffering one or more "Unaligned access" warnings when a call_shared
application is run. To test for this condition, set LD_LIBRARY_PATH to .:.
and run uname(1).

If for some reason it is not practical to remove the redundancy from the
LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable, this loader patch can be applied to
the system.


