jrecord@rhrsoft.com (Jim Record [RHR Software]) writes:

>       /usr/sbin/mount -t cdfs -r -o nodefperm /dev/rz5c /freeware

>This fails with : /dev/rz5c on /freeware: No such device

>I can mount the system CDROM and access it with bookreader
>without any problems.

>The system is brand new with the BASIC installation.

>Do I just have a bad CD?

>Any ideas?

Yes. You probably do not have the cdfs filesystem built into the
kernel.

Look in /sys/conf/<YOUR SYSTEM NAME IN CAPS> for the line:

options     CDFS

If it is not there, you cannot mount any cdfs aka ISO9660 cdroms

So, if it is missing, add it to the file and build a new kernel.
(See man doconfig for details)

Wilko

